  "result": "Perfect! All 83 tests pass. Here's a summary of the VAT implementation:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 1. **VAT Calculation** (`src/invoices.js`)\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- VAT is calculated **per line** on the amount **after discount**:\n  - lineAmount = qty \u00d7 unitPrice\n  - lineDiscount = lineAmount \u00d7 discountPercent / 100\n  - amountAfterDiscount = lineAmount - lineDiscount\n  - lineVat = **roundCents**(amountAfterDiscount \u00d7 vatRate / 100)\n- Invoice VAT = sum of all individually rounded line VATs\n- Formula: `total = subtotal - discount + vat` (clamped at 0)\n- Imported `roundCents` from `money.js` to ensure proper rounding per line\n\n### 2. **VAT Display in Render** (`src/render.js`)\n- Updated `renderInvoiceText()` to show VAT on its own line\n- VAT line appears just above the total\n- VAT line only shown if VAT > 0\n- Updated JSDoc to reflect VAT in output\n\n### 3. **Comprehensive Test Coverage**\n- Updated all 7 existing `invoiceTotals` tests to expect the new `vat` field\n- Added 5 new tests for VAT calculation:\n  - VAT on amount after discount\n  - Lines with different VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n  - VAT-exempt products (0% VAT)\n  - Rounding per line and summing\n- Updated all 7 render tests to expect VAT line in output\n- All 83 tests pass\n\n**Example calculation:**\n- Line: qty=5, unitPrice=8500, discount=10%, VAT=21%\n- Subtotal: \u20ac425.00\n- Discount: \u20ac42.50\n- Amount after discount: \u20ac382.50\n- VAT (21% on \u20ac382.50): \u20ac80.32 (rounded)\n- Total: \u20ac425.00 - \u20ac42.50 + \u20ac80.32 = **\u20ac462.82**",
